            "usage": "Fixed address 0x44. Use Wire at 100000 Hz with shared 3.3V supply/pull-ups; do not duplicate carrier 10kOhm pull-ups. Never issue heater commands. Wait >=1ms after power-up and >=8.3ms for high-repeatability measurement (10ms policy); busy reads NACK, no clock stretching. Validate 6-byte measurement CRC-8 (polynomial 0x31, initial 0xFF). Measurement <=0.5mA plus both 10kOhm +/-1% pull-ups at 3.6V is <1.23mA; 2mA peak is author margin, not heater capacity. Actual total bus capacitance/waveforms remain unverified unless supplied and measured; 100kHz alone does not prove timing. No powered bus driving an unpowered sensor, no 5V interface. Preserve airflow, avoid warm MCU/regulator placement; no final thermal/accuracy/manufacturing claim."
